    "note": "Introduced 2020-12-09. Struck: the misdemeanor penalty ($1,000 fine / up to one year, permit revoked five years), the sentence limiting item (10) violations to a Section 16-11-620 charge, and the cross-reference to 50-9-830. Added: civil fines of up to $200, then up to $500 and one-year permit revocation on a second violation within six months. The list of places in (M) is unchanged. The new text refers to a 'subsection (U)' that is not in the bill. Passage vote: none listed; introduced text only."
  },
  "operative_text": "Section 1 (Section 23-31-215(M)): A permit issued pursuant to this section does not authorize a permit holder to carry a concealable weapon into a:\nSection 1 (Section 23-31-215(M)): Except as provided for in subsection (U), a person found guilty of wilfully violating the provisions of this subsection shall be subject to a civil fine of not more than two hundred dollars. If a second violation occurs within a six-month period, the person shall be subject to a civil fine of not more than five hundred dollars and shall have his permit revoked for a period of one year. Imposition of fines pursuant to this subsection shall not give rise to any disability or legal disadvantage based on conviction for a criminal offense."
}